+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+Smooths the model's target curvature and adjusts how far ahead it looks when computing steering. When uncertainty about the lateral path a second ahead rises, including in curves, the smoothing time can triple up to 0.60 s.
+
+- Higher values smooth steering but may delay sharp curve entry or cause overshoot on exit.
+- At `1–2`, brief curvature spikes can cause rough steering or excessive torque buildup in a bend.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Each step is 0.01 s. If curve response feels slow, start by comparing `5–8` (0.05–0.08 s).
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
